    "hits": [
      {
        "block_id": "block-000064-ab2556c8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "reported_page": 3,
        "preview": " businesses — the largest of which is Google. We report Google in two segments, Google Services and Google Cloud, and all non-Google businesses collectively as Other Bets. Supporting these businesses, we have centralized certain AI-related research and development focused on advanced research in AI and developing the f"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block-000082-0ba57163",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "reported_page": 4,
        "preview": "For reporting purposes Google comprises two segments: Google Services and Google Cloud."
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block-000083-548f9d2e",
        "type": "heading_candidate",
        "reported_page": 4,
        "preview": "Google Services"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block-000085-7bd7f443",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "reported_page": 4,
        "preview": "ur services widely used, and our brand one of the most recognized in the world. Google Services' core products and platforms include ads, Android, Chrome, devices, Gmail, Google Drive, Google Gemini, Google Maps, Google Photos, Google Play, Search, and YouTube, with broad and growing adoption by users around the world."
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block-000093-0c7f9036",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "reported_page": 5,
        "preview": "Google Services generates revenues primarily by delivering both performance and brand advertising that appears on Google Search & other properties, YouTube, and Google Network partners' properties (\"Google Network properties\"). We continue "
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block-000097-b1521a49",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "reported_page": 5,
        "preview": "In addition, Google Services generates revenues from products and services beyond advertising, including:"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block-000167-360ccddc",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "reported_page": 10,
        "preview": "Within Google Services, we continue to invest heavily in devices, including our smartphones, home devices, and wearables, which is a highly competitive market with frequent introduction of new products and services, rapid adoption of technological"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block-000187-db4c8c6b",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "reported_page": 11,
        "preview": "ted to the success of our business. Maintaining and enhancing the brands within Google Services, Google Cloud, and Other Bets increases our ability to enter new categories and launch"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block-000397-132d42ca",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "reported_page": 28,
        "preview": " businesses — the largest of which is Google. We report Google in two segments, Google Services and Google Cloud, and all non-Google businesses collectively as Other Bets. Supporting these businesses, we have centralized certain AI-related research and development focused on advanced research in AI and developing the f"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block-000422-548f9d2e",
        "type": "heading_candidate",
        "reported_page": 29,
        "preview": "Google Services"
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block-000423-a9697220",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "reported_page": 29,
        "preview": "Google Services revenues consist of Google advertising as well as Google subscriptions, platforms, and devices revenues."
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block-000498-7f1a28ce",
        "type": "list_item",
        "reported_page": 32,
        "preview": " billion, an increase of 15% year over year, primarily driven by an increase in Google Services revenues of $37.8 billion, or 12%, and an increase in Google Cloud revenues of $15.5 billion, or 36%."
      }
    ],
